## Verified contract, without executing the package

Official Transformers tag `v5.15.1` resolves to commit
`550d7b3834670483a4df436541272c055dc364bf`. Two public source files were read in
memory, checked against their Git blob IDs, SHA-256 hashed and inspected as AST:

- [Package initialization](https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/550d7b3834670483a4df436541272c055dc364bf/src/transformers/__init__.py):
  41,736 bytes; Git blob `b932798ab46ec68af25ed41cac93c75e99902d42`;
  SHA-256 `f6609d7b595627749dc1f51205b504dd63211615f6a6c06cc70a6474d5edd597`.
- [Lazy-module implementation](https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/550d7b3834670483a4df436541272c055dc364bf/src/transformers/utils/import_utils.py):
  125,278 bytes; Git blob `dce7cad28fc979c6632be0b1482e18ffba74e1f0`;
  SHA-256 `ce7371afe0c1705a7f41a7528c590a1a6ae5bf23d9c307bdc19f9fdaedfe15fa`.

Initialization passes the declared version as an extra object to the replacement
lazy module. Its constructor stores extra objects separately; attribute access
returns them before any import branch. Thus a valid public version need not
appear directly in the replacement module dictionary. AST checks confirmed all
these structural facts without importing or executing either source file.

A minimal independent synthetic module reproduced the old false rejection and
passed with the corrected lookup. This establishes a real source-contract defect
in the old dictionary-only accessor. It does not inspect the actual failed image's
module dictionary, prove byte equality between release-tag files and installed
wheel members, or prove that subsequent native checks pass. The old diagnostic's
stale `origin_category=source` remains historical evidence, not a Transformers
path-origin failure. No old diagnostic or evidence was rewritten.

## Exactly one production expression changed

New, untracked successor `scripts/run_sft_oci_worker_probe_v2.py` differs from
the frozen v1 by precisely this expression substitution:

```diff
-str(vars(sys.modules[name]).get("__version__"))
+str(getattr(sys.modules[name], "__version__", None))
```

Every other byte is identical. In particular, the exact locked equality, `str`
conversion, missing-value default, failure code, complete installed distribution
map comparison, module roots, native identities, worker/fixture SHA, counters,
false flags and existing report schema remain unchanged. There is no metadata
fallback, accepted missing version, normalization, version range, swallowed
runtime error, lock change, path allowance or policy relaxation. The fresh v2
filename and source hash identify the correction; the wire schema did not change.

- Frozen v1: 22,633 bytes,
  `bed636e8cc08546a6be1b43c00c2f516fdc92dbf907dca674f7fb5aa7b5cb769`.
- New v2: 22,638 bytes,
  `b45b04fc9cb93dd2301df0444f2db95666ba4f7a32e8f4d8e28c5b4077314450`.
- New `tests/test_sft_oci_version_lookup_v2.py`:
  `855a8712a084fda9fa48eaa319e03d628a79f949a0feab18ff0ec2990000581a`.

Only three local files were added: v2 probe, its test module, and this receipt.
Existing builders, workflows and diagnostic source bindings still reference
their frozen versions. The v2 correction is deliberately not wired into a run.

